{
 "case": "N19-C08-NEG",
 "says": "The founder and Bora found Team A together. The founder is its only owner and its finalizer. The founder keeps one draft as a candidate on the laptop. The founder's own leave, even with the draft handed to Bora, is refused with last_owner_removal_refused, because it would remove the last owner and sole finalizer. A close whose plan names Bora as surviving owner, when no stewardship transfer to Bora has happened, is refused with succession_incomplete: naming an intended successor does not settle succession. A read then returns the same active state and both grants. The Team is archived. A continuation that names only a work scope and no existing work has no spelling and is refused at admission. A rename of the archived Team is refused with team_archived. The founder then closes it properly: the plan names the founder as surviving owner and keeps the draft on the laptop. The owner writes a closed state. On the closed Team, a recovery whose purpose is reopen is refused at admission, and a restore is refused with team_terminal. A read returns the closed state. Separately, the founder proposes Team B and cancels that unused founding. Bora's late acceptance of B's founding request is refused with team_terminal, and a read of B returns only its founding_cancelled state. No refused step returns a record, moves a head or changes a grant, and the draft stays with the laptop throughout.",
